                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 26 at 5:26PM HST until September 27 at 6:00AM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "Hurricane Nolo is now south-southwest of the Big Island and\nbeginning to move more quickly off to the west. The possibility of\nheavy rain could lead to localized flooding over portions of the Big\nIsland through tonight.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...The Big Island.\n\n* WHEN...Through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flood prone roads and other low lying areas may be closed\ndue to elevated runoff and overflowing streams. Urban areas may\nreceive more significant flooding and property damage due to rapid\nrunoff.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- The possibility remains for localized flooding over areas of the\nBig Island due to heavy rain from Hurricane Nolo to the\nsouth-southwest of the Big Island. Areas most at risk for\nflooding are the windward and southeast portions of the Big\nIsland where the ground remains saturated after recent rains.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
