                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 26 at 12:01PM MST until September 29 at 11:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive and long duration rainfall.\n\n* WHERE...All of northern and central Arizona.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday evening through Tuesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will be possible over burn areas, low-water\ncrossings, creeks, streams, washes and swimming holes. Larger\ncreeks and rivers may exceed bankfull. Flooding of paved roads and\nhighway underpasses will be possible. Unpaved roads could become\nmuddy and impassable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Low pressure will interact with tropical moisture from the\neastern Pacific. This could potentially produce numerous showers\nand embedded thunderstorms, with heavy rain that will fall over\nsaturated soils and burn scars. This could lead to localized\nflash flooding and rises on local rivers, such as the Little\nColorado River.\n- Additional information is available at weather.gov/flagstaff.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
