                "headline": "Flood Watch issued September 26 at 12:18PM EDT until September 29 at 2:00AM EDT by NWS Boston/Norton MA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Central and eastern Massachusetts as well as all of Rhode\nIsland.\n\n* WHEN...Through late Monday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nCreeks and streams may rise out of their banks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Periods of rain will continue across the region right through\nMonday. Storm total rainfall amount of 2-4\" are expected, but\nlocalized 5-7\" amounts are possible. If these higher amounts are\nrealized...the potential for both urban and small river/stream\nflooding would increase. This is particularly true if these\nlocalized higher amounts occur over a vulnerable urban center.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
